e1985905&quot;,&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Alistair Barr, global tech editor of Business Insider&quot;,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Alistair Barr, global tech editor of Business Insider, smiles at the camera while wearing a blue and white striped shirt.&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:1151,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;Business Insider&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1151},&quot;links&quot;:{&quot;self&quot;:&quot;https://i.insider.com/67e46b3b63d72727e1985905&quot;}}\">\n            \n          \n            <div>\n              <p>\n                  You're currently following this author!\n           Click to unsubscribe from email alerts.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n            \n          </span>\n            </p></div>\n        \n            <div>\n              <p><span>Alistair Barr is the driving force behind Business Insider's <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/category/ai-insider\">AI Insider</a> franchise, including the AI Insider newsletter. <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/subscription/newsletter/tech-memo\">Sign up here</a>. Before that, he was Business Insider's Global Tech Editor and the Big Tech team leader at Bloomberg, following a reporting career at The Wall Street Journal, USA Today, Reuters, and MarketWatch. Alistair covers all things Big Tech, along with startups and venture capital. He writes analysis and columns about topics including AI, cloud computing, data centers, semiconductors, online search, e-commerce, EVs, robotics, and autonomous vehicles.</span>\n              </p>\n              </div>\n          </div>\n    \n          \n          \n          \n          <div data-component-type=\"post-category-tags\" data-load-strategy=\"lazy\" data-track-marfeel=\"post-category-tags\">\n            <ul data-track-click-shared=\"{&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:&quot;navigation&quot;,&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;category_link&quot;}\">\n                \n                <li>\n                  <a data-track-click=\"\" href=\"/category/artificial-intelligence\" title=\"Artificial Intelligence\">Artificial Intelligence</a>\n                </li>      \n                <li>\n                  <a data-track-click=\"\" href=\"/category/anthropic\" title=\"Anthropic\">Anthropic</a>\n                </li>      \n                <li>\n                  <a data-track-click=\"\" href=\"/category/ai-insider\" title=\"AI Insider\">AI Insider</a>\n                </li>\n                <li>\n                  <span data-track-click=\"{&quot;click_text&quot;:&quot;More&quot;,&quot;click_path&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\">More </span>\n                </li>\n          \n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n    \n    \n          <section data-track-page-area=\"Post Bottom\">\n          <!-- Included desktop \"taboola\" -->    <vendor-taboola data-component-type=\"vendor-taboola\" data-root-margin=\"0px 0px 100% 0px\" data-consent=\"MARKETING\" config=\"{&quot;providerName&quot;:&quot;taboola&quot;,&quot;providerPageType&quot;:{&quot;article&quot;:&quot;auto&quot;},&quot;providerUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn.taboola.com/libtrc/businessinsider/loader.js&quot;,&quot;providerPrivacyLoader&quot;:&quot;https://static.tblcontent.com/libtrc/businessinsider/loader.privacy.js&quot;,&quot;providerPixel&quot;:&quot;https://static.qovani.com/libtrc/tr5?type=pixel&publisher=businessinsider&quot;,&quot;providerFlushValue&quot;:{&quot;flush&quot;:true},&quot;providerData&quot;:{&quot;mode&quot;:&quot;thumbs-1r&quot;,&quot;container&quot;:&quot;taboola-below-main-column&quot;,&quot;placement&quot;:&quot;Below Article Thumbnails Logged Out&quot;,&quot;target_type&quot;:&quot;mix&quot;}}\" data-load-strategy=\"defer\">\n                \n              </vendor-taboola>\n          \n          <!-- Excluded mobile \"taboola\" --></section>\n    \n      </section>\n  </section>\n\n  \n  \n\n\n    <back-to-home data-component-type=\"back-to-home\" data-load-strategy=\"defer\" data-only-on=\"mobile\">\n      \n  \n      \n  \n      \n    </back-to-home>\n</section></DIV>","content_text":"Anthropic's internal AI use, valued at retail prices, now exceeds its employee pay By Alistair Barr You're currently following this author! Click to unsubscribe from email alerts. Author of the AI Insider newsletter Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei. Aaron Schwartz/Bloomberg via Getty Images Here's a remarkable milestone in the AI revolution: Anthropic now spends more on internal AI usage than it does paying employees.The company revealed this in its IPO filing. In April, the value of Claude AI used internally, calculated at prices Anthropic charges customers, exceeded its monthly employee compensation costs, excluding stock awards. By September, that internal AI usage had surged more than 250-fold since January.There's an important distinction here. Anthropic isn't actually spending more cash on AI than salaries. It's valuing its internal AI consumption at retail prices.Still, this feels like a watershed moment for the tech industry.In March, I wrote about a new trend: Tech companies are starting to treat AI tokens (the main way to measure usage) as a fourth component of employee compensation, alongside salary, bonuses, and stock awards.Anthropic's numbers show why. More than 90% of the code added to its software in September was written by Claude. Meanwhile, revenue has grown vastly faster than headcount.For decades, talented humans were the most valuable resource in Silicon Valley. Now AI is challenging that assumption.Sign up for the AI Insider newsletter here. Reach out to me via email at abarr@businessinsider.com Read next Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Alistair Barr You're currently following this author! Click to unsubscribe from email alerts. Alistair Barr is the driving force behind Business Insider's AI Insider franchise, including the AI Insider newsletter. Sign up here. Before that, he was Business Insider's Global Tech Editor and the Big Tech team leader at Bloomberg, following a reporting career at The Wall Street Journal, USA Today, Reuters, and MarketWatch. Alistair covers all things Big Tech, along with startups and venture capital. He writes analysis and columns about topics including AI, cloud computing, data centers, semiconductors, online search, e-commerce, EVs, robotics, and autonomous vehicles. Artificial Intelligence Anthropic AI Insider More","fetched_at":"2026-11-02T10:11:48.986Z","ok":true}